        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Summarizes how the methods behind the report's estimates of hepatitis incidence, prevalence, mortality and diagnosis and treatment coverage have changed since the 2017 and 2024 reports, chiefly a full recalibration of the HBV and HCV models with the Center for Disease Analysis Foundation that revises past figures, so earlier estimates should not be compared with these. Notes, for example, that HBV prevalence among children under five in 2020 is now put at 0.65% rather than 0.9%, that the 2015 baseline of 6–10 million new infections has been revised downwards, and that time series for 2015–2024 are now provided. Explains that country maps and target assessments rely on modelled estimates, which should prompt national review rather than serve as official proof of elimination, describes how the HBV and HCV cascades of care are presented, and announces updated online country profiles.",
